ock (1a) fitted, undo the bolts (1b) and remove\nthe engine flywheel (1c).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1a</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.161.001</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001956.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Refit the engine flywheel  in its housing\nand secure by tightening the bolts to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FLYWHEEL</p></td><td><p>M12</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Crankshaft side) 14.4 ÷ 17.6</p></td></tr></table></div>"],[4,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Fit the flywheel lock.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.779.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Undo the bolts (2a) and remove the engine flywheel (2b).</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The engine flywheel retaining\nbolts are treated with a compound to prevent them coming undone\nthey should therefore be replaced whenever they are removed.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2047951.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the flywheel (1a) back in its housing and fix it tightening\nthe bolts (1b) to the recommended torque.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The engine flyhwheel may only\nbe refitted in one position because the retaining bolt holes are not\nequidistant.</p></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The engine flywheel retaining\nbolts are treated with a compound to prevent them coming undone\nthey should therefore be replaced whenever they are removed.</p></aside><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FLYWHEEL</p></td><td><p>M12</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Crankshaft side) 2.9 ÷ 3.2 + 48 ÷ 51</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Use the tool for angular tightening of\nthe engine flywheelbolts.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Protractor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.942.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Remove the flywheel lock.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.779.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2047952.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Position a suitable flywheel lock for stopping the rotation of\nthe actual flywheel.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.820.624.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Undo the bolts (2a) and remove the engine flywheel (2b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002243.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Fit the flywheel in the crankshaft housing.</p><p>Screw in the bolts and then tighten to\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><tabl